; MiSTer RTG -- mmu.library configuration
;
; Append these two lines to ENVARC:MMU-Configuration (and copy to ENV:, or
; reboot).  mmu.library reads the file when it initialises, which is before
; SetPatch installs 68040.library, so the regions are already tagged by the
; time anything builds a page table.
;
; WHY THIS IS NEEDED
;
; Every other graphics board in the stock MMU-Configuration is declared with
; a "For <manufacturer> <product>" clause, because AutoConfig gave it a
; ConfigDev and mmu.library can find it by ID.  The MiSTer RTG board has no
; ConfigDev at all: MiSTer.card.asm hardcodes REGISTER_BASE $b80100 and
; MEMORY_BASE $02000000 and never calls FindConfigDev, so expansion.library
; never learns the board exists.  With nothing to tag, mmu.library leaves
; both regions marked Blank -- address space it believes holds nothing --
; and MuScan shows exactly that:
;
;   0x00A80000 - 0x00BBFFFF  Blank WriteThrough          <- the registers
;   0x00BC0000 - 0x00BFFFFF  CacheInhibit I/O space      <- real I/O, tagged
;   0x02000000 - 0x027FFFFF  Imprecise NonSerial Blank   <- the framebuffer
;
; On a CPU without an MMU the hardcoded addresses simply work, which is why
; RTG is fine on the stock TG68K core.  On the 040 the pages are not mapped,
; so every register access faults -- reading the RTG ID at $B8010E gives
; $0000 where the hardware returns $5001 -- and every pixel write goes
; nowhere.  Hence: works before SetPatch, black screen after it.
;
; Since there is no ConfigDev to match on, these use literal addresses rather
; than {base}.  Standalone SetCacheMode is supported for exactly this case.
;
; The flags follow what the stock file uses for every other board: a register
; block is Valid IOSpace CacheInhibit (cache-inhibited SERIALIZED, so ordering
; is preserved across register writes), and video memory adds NonSerial
; Imprecise for fast uncached writes.  Compare the VA2000 entry, which splits
; the same way.  Note the framebuffer already reads back as Imprecise
; NonSerial above -- the only thing being changed there is Blank -> Valid
; IOSpace.
;
; Addresses come from MiSTer.card.asm: REGISTER_BASE $b80100 lives in the 4K
; page fastchip decodes at $B80000-$B80FFF (addr[23:12] == 'hB80, palette
; included), and MEMORY_BASE $02000000 with MEMORY_SIZE $800000.  Both are
; page aligned at the 4K page size MuScan reports.

;MiSTer RTG registers ($B80000-$B80FFF: control block and CLUT)
SetCacheMode	0x00b80000	0x00001000	Valid IOSpace CacheInhibit

;MiSTer RTG framebuffer (MEMORY_BASE, MEMORY_SIZE = 8MB)
SetCacheMode	0x02000000	0x00800000	Valid IOSpace CacheInhibit NonSerial Imprecise
